Self-test clip: sources and licence

selftest.opus, reference.txt and truth.json are installed with Fluentfolio. `fluentfolio self-test` runs the
clip through every part that is installed and switched on, and checks the results against these files.

selftest.opus
  A 58 s exchange of two readers from LibriSpeech test-clean: speaker 1089 asks twice (utterances
  1089-134686-0001 and 1089-134686-0003), and speaker 121 answers each time with several sentences
  (121-121726-0000, -0001, -0003, -0007, -0009, -0010 and 121-123859-0004).
  LibriSpeech ASR corpus, Vassil Panayotov, Guoguo Chen, Daniel Povey and Sanjeev Khudanpur, 2015.
  https://www.openslr.org/12
  Licence: CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Changes: level raised to -20 dBFS active speech (peak at most -6 dBFS), inner silences longer than 100 ms
  shortened to 100 ms, a -75 dBFS dither added, the utterances laid out on one timeline with pauses between
  them and a quiet noise floor, and encoded as 16 kHz mono Ogg Opus. tools/selftest_clip.py makes it.

reference.txt
  The corpus transcripts of the nine utterances, in time order.

truth.json
  Where each utterance starts and ends, who speaks it, the total speech time, and the median pitch of the
  reader who answers, measured with Praat on the encoded clip. They are derived from the corpus under the
  same licence.
